Z||000000||Formula 18||07-30-2001||01:56 PM||||OK I called local parts shop and they told me that there was no such thing as a dog-bone or a torque strut listed for Fieros.. <BR>OK You're no help...That little Alum. thingy must not really be there... <P>Then called Fiero store Sorry we don't carry bushing for an 88 v6 just the earlier years but I will sell you a 50 dollar replacemnet dogbone... Again no help. I am on a budget here. <P>My question is can I just get a dogbone of an 85 or something a get poly bushings for that and put it in the Formula??<BR>If I can anyone want to give me there old dog-bone?? Better yet anyone have a good one?? I'll front shipping... ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-30-2001||03:14 PM||||AFAIK, you can use an earlier year dog bone, and just replace the bushings. Sorry, I don't have one laying around.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
